  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Nebularine and the Prostaglandin E2 receptor EP4 subtype, mediated through G2/mitotic-specific cyclin B1. Nebularine is identified as a target of two distinct compounds, (5R,19R)-11-ethyl-19-hydroxy-5-methyl-18-methylidene-9-oxa-11-azaheptacyclo[15.2.1.01,14.02,12.04,13.05,10.08,13]icosan-16-one and (1S)-2-Cyclohexen-1-ol, both of which are linked to the EP4 receptor. This indicates that Nebularine may interact with the EP4 receptor through these intermediates, suggesting a possible mechanism of action involving cyclin B1. The scores for both pathways are consistent, reinforcing the likelihood of a functional connection. However, the exact nature of the interaction remains uncertain, and further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct relationship between Nebularine and the EP4 receptor.",
